Linear DC sweep of source voltage across a divider

// Hand translation of ../circuit.sp, line for line:
//
//   V1 in 0 DC 0     ->  v1 (in 0) v dc=0
//   R1 in out 1k     ->  r1 (in out) r r=1k
//   R2 out 0 3k      ->  r2 (out 0) r r=3k
//   .dc V1 0 10 0.5  ->  sweep ... from=0 to=10 points=20 + analysis op
//
// VACASK has no `.dc`: a DC sweep is a `sweep` block around an operating
// point. Its `points` counts INTERVALS, so `.dc`'s 21 points (0 to 10 step
// 0.5) is points=20 — off by one here and every sample lands between two of
// ngspice's and the whole column reads as a phantom error.
//
// The sweep variable is named `vsweep` because VACASK identifiers cannot
// contain `-`: it is the same scale ngspice and espice call `v(v-sweep)`, and
// the runner's scale_aliases maps the one spelling onto the other.

ground 0

load "resistor.osdi"

model r resistor
model v vsource

v1 (in 0) v dc=0
r1 (in out) r r=1k
r2 (out 0) r r=3k

control
  options rawfile="binary"
  sweep vsweep instance="v1" parameter="dc" from=0 to=10 mode="lin" points=20
    analysis dc1 op
endc
